Nested while loop in Python
A nested while loop means writing one while loop inside another while loop.
- Outer while loop: Controls how many times the inner loop executes.
- Inner while loop: Executes completely for every iteration of the outer loop.
1. Basic syntax
while condition1:    # Outer loop statements    while condition2:        # Inner loop statements



2. Simple example
i = 1while i <= 3:    print("Outer loop:", i)    j = 1    while j <= 3:        print("Inner loop:", j)        j += 1    i += 1



